<!-- SECTION 15A: LEGAL FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal Framework</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>IT Act 2000:</strong> S.2(1)(p): defines digital signature. S.3: authentication via DSC. S.35: CA issues DSC. S.73A: electronic signature. DSC = same legal validity as handwritten.</p><p><strong>CCA:</strong> Regulates licensed CAs. Class 3 only since Jan 2021. Video verification mandatory. Cloud DSC approved. Licensed CAs: eMudhra, Sify, nCode, NSDL, Capricorn, CSC.</p><p><strong>Companies Act 2013 + MCA21:</strong> All MCA filings require DSC: SPICe+, AOC-4, MGT-7, DIR-3 KYC, CHG-1, SH-7.</p><p><strong>Income Tax Act:</strong> Companies, audit-liable firms/LLPs, political parties must use DSC for ITR.</p><p><strong>CGST Act 2017:</strong> Companies/LLPs: DSC for GST registration and GSTR-1/3B/9. Proprietors: eSign alternative.</p><p><strong>Portals:</strong> <a href="https://mca.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MCA</a> | <a href="https://incometax.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Income Tax</a> | <a href="https://gst.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GST</a> | <a href="https://cca.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CCA</a></p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

