                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is DSC and why is it needed in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>DSC is the electronic equivalent of a physical signature, legally valid under IT Act 2000. Mumbai businesses need it for: MCA filings with RoC Mumbai (500,000+ companies), GST registration/returns (companies/LLPs), income tax e-filing (audit-liable entities), and e-tendering (GeM/CPPP). Without DSC, a company cannot file annual returns or register for GST.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does DSC cost in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Class 3 Sign Only (1 yr): Rs 1,500-2,000. Sign Only (2 yr): Rs 2,000-2,800. Sign & Encrypt (2 yr): Rs 2,800-3,500. Sign & Encrypt (3 yr): Rs 3,500-5,500. USB token: Rs 500-800 (one-time). Cloud DSC: Rs 2,000-3,000. Foreign director: Rs 5,000-8,000. Portal registration: Rs 500-1,000/portal. Bulk 5+: 10-15% discount.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What documents are required for DSC?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Indian nationals: PAN card (mandatory, name must match exactly), Aadhaar (for eKYC video), passport-size photo, active email, active mobile. NRIs/foreign: passport, PAN (if available), foreign address proof, Embassy attestation or apostille. Company signatory: additionally board resolution. Patron verifies PAN name before application.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does DSC issuance take?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Indian nationals with Aadhaar: same-day at Marine Lines (by 2 PM) to max 2 working days. NRIs/foreign nationals: 3-5 working days (attestation dependent). Renewal: same-day. Portal registration: 30-60 minutes per portal. Walk-in with on-site video verification.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is Class 3 DSC mandatory for MCA and GST?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Class 3 is the only class since Jan 2021 (Class 1/2 phased out). MCA: all filings by directors, LLP partners, CAs, CSs require Class 3. GST: companies/LLPs must use DSC for registration and returns. Proprietors can use Aadhaar eSign for GST. Income Tax: companies and audit-liable entities must use DSC.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What if my DSC is not working or emSigner fails?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Common issues: emSigner not detecting token (install correct driver), browser blocking emSigner (allow Java/security exceptions), PAN mismatch (name must match exactly), expired DSC (renew immediately), token PIN locked (reset via CA tool), certificate chain error (install intermediate CA certificate). Patron provides remote desktop troubleshooting within 30 minutes.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
